 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Decorator:** `needs_app_scope`, defined in `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It loads the app and pushes `app.app_context()` before your callback runs. It skips this if an app is already active.\n\nYou often don't need to apply it yourself. Commands registered with `@app.cli.command()` or `@bundle.cli.command()` get wrapped automatically, because those groups are `AppGroup` instances (`src/tessel/app.py:338`, `src/tessel/bundles.py:49`). Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to opt out. If you use a plain `@click.command()`, add `@needs_app_scope` yourself.\n\n**Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`), through its `load_app()` method (`cli.py:333`). `needs_app_scope` calls it via `ctx.ensure_object(LaunchInfo).load_app()` (`cli.py:397`). `TesselGroup` (`cli.py:531`) is the top-level group that creates `LaunchInfo`. It is not the same as `AppGroup` (`cli.py:405`).",
